// The client function interpreter (function AMM redesign §6/§7.1 — the JS half of the durable execution engine).
//
// This mirrors the SERVER interpreter (Platform.Core/Function/Tree/FunctionInterpreter.cs): an EXPLICIT heap stack
// of frames (NOT the JS call stack), driven by a step loop, so execution can be suspended and serialized at any
// point — the precondition for the cross-side hand-off (await a Side=Server call → suspend → post the continuation
// to the server) and the language-neutral continuation the two halves pass back and forth. P2-a builds the pure-
// execution core (control flow + expressions + local assignment + return); async data effects + the hand-off land
// in later P2 slices, exactly as the server half evolved (3a → 3b → 4).

