          // rules (D71): a value that cannot possibly be accepted is refused HERE, raising the same
          // ValidationException — with the same per-field Violations — that the server would have raised. So the app's
          // `catch (ValidationException ex)` handles a local refusal and a server refusal identically, and the user
          // sees the message under the offending field instantly instead of after a doomed trip to the server.
          //
          // NOT the gate, and deliberately incomplete (see validate-delta.ts): the server still validates every write
          // it receives, and it still has the last word — a slug taken between this check and the commit is refused
          // there, not here.
          // The user has now TRIED to save, so a form may reveal every violation — including on fields they never
          // visited (the browser does exactly this on submit). Before that, only the fields they have LEFT are shown.
          root.markSaveAttempted();
