// U5 slices 2+3 (+ "Rec") — the CSR render walker: ComponentTree (the wire JSON from GET /ui/{name}) → live DOM,
// now with KEYED RECONCILIATION. The walker builds a VNode tree (render/reconcile.ts) and DIFFS it against the
// retained previous tree, so a change patches only what moved — editing one row of a 500-row list touches one node,
// not all 500 (the old wholesale replaceChildren was an explicit interim). A bound <input> is reused across renders,
// so focus/caret survive naturally (no save/restore dance).
//
// Slice scope (honest bounds, each loud where it ends):
//   • Structure: Element / Component (recursive, fetched via ComponentSource) / Text / If–else chains / Foreach
//     over scope values / Fragment. Slot throws (the layout slice owns it).
//   • Reactivity: state initializers evaluate at mount; `setState` re-renders (now reconciled, not rebuilt). derived
//     evaluates on read with a cycle guard. A child component instance PERSISTS across a parent re-render (keyed by
//     its build path) — its state/queries survive; it contributes its rendered VNodes inline and delegates its
//     re-renders to the root, which reconciles the whole tree.
//   • Data (slice 3): a Query member gets a QueryHandle bound to its rootId — the fetch goes through the server's
//     GET /{ctx}/query/{rootId} read, rows land in the SharedStore, the member reads as a QUERY VIEW.
//     A `live` member subscribes the change channel; a signal → refetch → re-render. A store change also
//     re-renders — items read THROUGH the store. Without a RenderData context a query member reads null.
//   • Events/actions: an event prop (onClick: save) wires the action to a DOM listener; the listener is re-pointed on
//     patch so a re-render never fires a stale closure.
//
// Atom → DOM mapping: the platform ships only a FEW native primitives, so the map is a small explicit table; an
// unknown atom renders as <div data-osy-element="Name">. Non-DOM props (styling) are recorded as data-osy-* until the
// token/variant CSS system (U5b) replaces that interim. The SSR renderer (Platform.Core/Ui/UiServerRenderer.cs)
// mirrors this mapping exactly so a future hydration attaches to the server DOM cleanly.

